ok file new() makes an open handle
ok file append() adds a last line, lines counted from 1
ok file insert(n, x) puts x at line n and moves the rest down
ok file replace(n, x) changes line n
ok file replace(a, b) changes the text a to b
ok file index_of() is the line that is exactly x, or 0
ok file search() is the first line that holds x
ok file contains() asks for a whole line
ok file first and last
ok file close() answers true, the handle is not ok after it, and open() opens it again
ok file satellite.file.open() reads what close() saved
ok file a newline inside append() makes two lines
ok file remove_at(n) and remove(x) take lines out
ok file remove_first() and remove_last()
ok file truncate(n) keeps the first n lines
ok file clear() leaves no lines
ok file save() puts the change on the disk for another handle
ok file new() over a file that is there is not ok
ok file open() of a missing file is not ok, and never makes it
ok file satellite.file.clear() empties the file and leaves it there
ok file ends a last line that had no newline before it appends
ok file keeps a file's \r\n endings when it appends (od reads 0d 0a)
ok file a method written after satellite.file.new(...) runs
ok file handed to a capsule is the caller's file
ok file lock(): two threads appending to one file lose nothing
ok file closed through one name is closed for both
ok file nothing is left beside the program
